## Enriching code metadata with suMEDS

External-ontology work lives in [suMEDS](https://github.com/rvandewater/suMEDS), not in this ETL. The
package ships its rules,
[`src/{{ package_name }}/sumeds_rules.yaml`](src/{{ package_name }}/sumeds_rules.yaml), registered in
suMEDS's `sumeds.rules` entry-point group under the spec's name, `{{ dataset_name }}`, so
`--rules {{ dataset_name }}` works for any suMEDS command, and the spec's `sumeds_enrich` stage applies
them.

`metadata/dataset.json` says whether a build is enriched: `sumeds_enrichment.enriched` is `true` (with
the rules, pack source and coverage) or `false` (with the error and the `retry` command):

```bash
jq .sumeds_enrichment.enriched $MEDS_OUTPUT_DIR/metadata/dataset.json
```

Enrichment soft-fails: without internet access, say, the ETL still succeeds with
`metadata/codes.parquet` as MEDS-Extract wrote it. The warning, with the command that finishes the
enrichment, is in `$MEDS_OUTPUT_DIR/.logs/pipeline.log`. Running `meds-extract-run` again does not retry
the stage; `suMEDS-enrich` does:

```bash
suMEDS-enrich $MEDS_OUTPUT_DIR
# Air-gapped: from a copy of the sumeds-ontologies packs directory
suMEDS-enrich $MEDS_OUTPUT_DIR --ontology-source /path/to/sumeds-ontologies/ontologies --offline
# The plain, unenriched ETL
meds-extract-run spec={{ dataset_name }} output_dir=$MEDS_OUTPUT_DIR skip_stages=[sumeds_enrich]
# Make a failed enrichment fail the run
meds-extract-run spec={{ dataset_name }} output_dir=$MEDS_OUTPUT_DIR "overrides=['++stage_cfg.strict=true']"
```

Enrichment never overwrites what the ETL wrote: descriptions and `parent_codes` stay, and new parents
are appended.

